	spec: "The web composer's pause/play button (task v0g) is always present. Busy, it pauses; paused, it continues. Idle, it shows the play icon named Continue (caption 'Ask the model to keep going.') and is enabled when the session is idle and the draft is empty, regardless of the last transcript entry, including an empty session with its synthetic greeting (user correction 2026-10-08); pressing it sends one prompt picked at random from a short list of nudges (src/common/states.ts NUDGES: 'Continue.', 'Proceed.', 'Go on.', 'Keep going.', 'Carry on.', 'Go ahead.', 'Finish it.', 'You can do it.', 'Onward!': a few words each, asking for action rather than another plan; user request 2026-10-07), sent and shown like a typed prompt. With a draft it stays disabled: the host clears a draft its prompt contains, so a nudge could swallow a draft such as 'Go'. Composer action buttons draw their keyboard focus ring inside (outline-offset -2px), so the composer edge and the caption never clip it (user request 2026-10-07). Plain Enter on an empty idle terminal prompt sends a nudge from the same shared pool through ordinary draft submission, including empty sessions and sessions ending with command output (user approval 2026-10-08). Modified Enter, busy sessions, paused/error continuation, typed prompts and prompt editing retain their behavior. Web empty-input Enter is unchanged.",
